1470. Shuffle the Array

Description:
Given an array nums containing two halves [x1,x2,...,xn,y1,y2,...,yn], rearrange it by taking one element from each half alternately:

[x1,y1,x2,y2,...,xn,yn]

Test Case:

Input:  nums = [2,5,1,3,4,7], n = 3
Output: [2,3,5,4,1,7]

Why?

First half:  [2,5,1]
Second half: [3,4,7]

Take alternately:
2 → 3 → 5 → 4 → 1 → 7

So the answer is [2,3,5,4,1,7].

class Solution {
    public int[] shuffle(int[] nums, int n) {
        int[] arr= new int[nums.length];
        int i=0,j=n,k=0;
        while(i<n){
            arr[k]=nums[i];
            arr[k+1]=nums[j];
            i++;
            j++;
            k=k+2;
        }
        return arr;
    }
}
